urce":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:652418af314f2b004c6a71a08e7d134b308316d01bd25f5825a42b3fd54bd712","file":"preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex","line":37,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8cc283a10def0f9fb7e549e81994f644d53a79359fee0d69afdf6eaf909ae5c2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:652418af314f2b004c6a71a08e7d134b308316d01bd25f5825a42b3fd54bd712","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Parabolic-intersections-in-Artin-groups-September-23-2026/build/sections/01_intro.tex#L37"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:arbitrary-intersections}\nFor every family $\\mathcal F$ of parabolic subgroups of $A$, there is a\nsubfamily $\\mathcal F_0\\subseteq\\mathcal F$ with $|\\mathcal F_0|\\le |S|$ such\nthat\n\\[\n \\bigcap_{P\\in\\mathcal F}P=\\bigcap_{P\\in\\mathcal F_0}P.\n\\]\nHere the intersection of an empty family is $A$. In particular, arbitrary\nintersections of parabolic subgroups are parabolic, and every subset\n$E\\subseteq A$ is contained in a unique smallest parabolic subgroup."}
